hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"930","We are Abu Muhammad Fahd bin Sulaiman Al-Masry. We are Abu Tawbah, meaning Al-Rabi’ bin Nafi’. Muawiyah, who is Ibn Salam, narrated to us on the authority of Zaid. Ibn Salam, that Abu Salam told him, Al-Harith Al-Ash’ari told me, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, told them, he said: “Indeed, God Almighty has commanded Yahya bin Zakariya gave five words that he acted upon, and commanded the Children of Israel to act upon them. He said: He was slow with them, so Jesus said to him: You have been commanded with five words to act upon, and you command the Children of Israel to act upon them. Either you command them to act upon them, or I will do them. So he ordered them to do them, and Yahya said: If you precede me with them, I fear that I will be punished or that I will be humiliated. So he gathered the children of Israel in the Holy House until The mosque was filled, until people sat on the balconies, so he preached to the people, then he said: God Almighty has commanded me with five words that I will implement, and I command you to Act upon them, the first of which is that you do not associate anything with God, for whoever associates anything with God is like a man who bought a slave out of his own money. With gold or paper, then he said to him: This is my home and my work, so work for me and give me your work. So he started working and gave his work to someone other than his master. Which of you would love to have a servant like that, performing his work for someone other than his master, and it is God who created you and provided for you, so do not associate anything with God. And he said: God Almighty has commanded you to pray, so when you set your faces, do not turn away, for God sets his face to the face of His servant when he prays. He will pray for him, and he will not turn his face away from him until the servant is turning away.” And he mentioned the hadith in its entirety."
